Before text blocks: String json = "{
  "name": "Java"
}"; — error-prone, hard to read. With text blocks: String json = """
  {
    "name": "Java"
  }
  """; — clean and readable. Text blocks are semantically equivalent to string literals — they produce a String at runtime, work with all String methods, can be used anywhere a String is accepted, and support .formatted() for interpolation.

