8. Rewrite this code to fix the bug:
class UserValidator {
    public boolean validate(String role) {
        String allowedRole = "ADMIN";
        if (role == allowedRole) {
            return true;
        }
        return false;
    }
}

items.a:
The bug: using == instead of equals() for string comparison. == compares references — if role and allowedRole happen to point to the same pool object, it returns true, but if role comes from external input (HTTP request, DB query, etc.), it's a heap string and == returns false even for "ADMIN".

Fixed:
class UserValidator {
    public boolean validate(String role) {
        return "ADMIN".equals(role);  // Yoda condition — null-safe
    }
}

// Or more explicitly:
// return role != null && role.equals("ADMIN");
// Or with null-safety:
// return Objects.equals(role, "ADMIN");
